 ### Distance Estimator
-A Distance Estimator is a function that computes the minimum distance from a query point to *any* object in a scene, often returning the distance along with the identifier or color of the closest object [S19, unofficial]. It initializes the minimum distance to a maximum draw distance (e.g., 1000) and iterates through scene primitives, updating the minimum if a closer object is found [S19, unofficial]. This avoids recomputing color lookups for the endpoint later [S19, unofficial]. While the Sphere SDF returns the distance to a *single* sphere, a Distance Estimator aggregates multiple SDFs (including the Sphere SDF) to find the global minimum [S19, unofficial].
+A Distance Estimator is a function that computes the minimum distance from a query point to *any* object in a scene, often returning the distance along with the identifier or color of the closest object [S20, unofficial]. It initializes the minimum distance to a maximum draw distance (e.g., 1000) and iterates through scene primitives, updating the minimum if a closer object is found [S20, unofficial]. This avoids recomputing color lookups for the endpoint later [S20, unofficial]. While the Sphere SDF returns the distance to a *single* sphere, a Distance Estimator aggregates multiple SDFs (including the Sphere SDF) to find the global minimum [S20, unofficial].
 
